      "problem": "Consider a $9\\times 4$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A))=2,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}({A}^{T}))=$",
      "worked_solution": "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14273966/assets/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=9,$ $n=4,$ and $r=2.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}({A}^{T})) & =m-r=9-2=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
